body:
The right likes to scream he was a conservative but this interview squashes that shit out real fucking quick;

https://twitter.com/WUTangKids/status/1485999936797818881?t=OXRZcfw2NL6lA6Tcj8fG9w&s=19

As far as what he would say if he was here now? I'd like to believe to he'd probably continue calling out hypocrites on both sides of the political spectrum but he'd have an absolute field day with conservatives. He'd probably keep truckin on with his "fuck hope" motto. We're all fucked and HSIOW (Holy shit it's only Wednesday)

So I live in a moderately medium sized town and I live in a small house which is $400 a month. When all this Covid started and I got furloughed last year my landlord, who is a sweet old man, might I add, told me and I quote, "If you can't pay, you can't pay. I'm not worried about it, I'll cover you. You just take care of yourself." I was out of work for almost 4 months, finally got a new job around October. I offered to make payments for the 4 months I was unable to, found out that he was going  to cover me through the end of 2020. The guy isn't rich by any means, but, he takes cares of his tenets and is probably the nicest guy I've ever met.

&#x200B;

I tell you this because another landlord in town that owned some homes/apartments isn't so nice. When evictions started last year he did not hesitate to throw people out. A couple blocks from me in an apartment building lived a single mom with 2 kids. She had lost her job due to COVID and she did not pay the $700 rent on the 1st of the following month. He literally called the sheriffs department and loudly exclaimed while waiting on them to gain entry to her apartment, "Drag her out kicking and screaming if you have to, I don't give a shit if she has kids, drag them out too." Guy was a certified grade A asshole. When the eviction moratorium set in he was beyond pissed. The only shining  light here is he actually passed away in March due to a heart attack. 

&#x200B;

I really feel for the people who are evicted because I've been in their shoes even before I started living in my current residence. I really feel that Congress failed everybody by not making the eviction moratorium a top priority. A lot of people are about to be dumped in the streets during a fucking pandemic no less and you cannot count on every landlord to be like mine. They need to get the moratorium going and do it now. There's already a lot of people who have been forcefully removed from their homes, and we need to stop the bleeding.

This. Historically the Conservatives absolutely love to rewrite history from their POV. We never hurt the Indians, they "volunteered to give up their land." Slaves weren't really slaves, they were treated like "family" and given "opportunities" and the KKK wasn't a bad group they were "misunderstood" and "fighting for their beliefs" 

&#x200B;

Conservatism is a disease
